## Summary
- Slides can now define a playable `animation` with `play(el)` and `stop(el)` — the toolbar shows a play/stop toggle button only when the current slide has one
- Navigating away from a slide automatically stops any running animation
- Slide sizing is now `aspect-ratio: 16/9` scaled to fit the viewport, so the toolbar is always visible on any screen size without scrolling
- Font sizes use `cqw` container-query units so they scale with the slide element
- Updated `02-demo.js` to demonstrate a looping `requestAnimationFrame` wave animation

## Animation API
```js
Deck.slide({
  animation: {
    play(el) {
      const frame = requestAnimationFrame(/* ... */);
      el._stop = () => cancelAnimationFrame(frame);
    },
    stop(el) {
      if (el._stop) el._stop();
    },
  },
});
```

